# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this and renders a "Cite this repository" button.
#
# REVIEW BEFORE PUBLISHING:
#   - `authors` below is derived from the git history (commit counts) and lists names
#     exactly as they appear there. Confirm who should be credited as an author of the
#     software, in what order, and add ORCIDs / affiliations where you have them.
#   - `repository-code` and `url` point at the public repository; update them once it
#     exists.
#   - Bump `version` and `date-released` when you tag a release.
#   - If there is a paper to cite instead of the software, add a `preferred-citation`
#     block and people will be pointed at that.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EchoFrame: ultrafast GPU functional ultrasound imaging library"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  EchoFrame is a CUDA-accelerated library for real-time plane-wave ultrasound
  imaging. It provides Fourier-domain beamforming and Power Doppler Imaging (PDI)
  pipelines written in C++17/CUDA, with MATLAB (MEX) and Python (pybind11)
  bindings, aimed at functional ultrasound imaging (fUSI).
authors:
  - family-names: Florescu
    given-names: Stefanos
  - family-names: Demi
    given-names: Arber
  - family-names: Kruizinga
    given-names: Pieter
  - family-names: Le Meur-Diebolt
    given-names: Samuel
  - family-names: Krumin
    given-names: Michael
  - family-names: Andela
    given-names: Bouwe
version: 1.0
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/BrainEchoLab/EchoFrame"
url: "https://github.com/BrainEchoLab/EchoFrame"
keywords:
  - functional ultrasound
  - fUSI
  - ultrasound imaging
  - beamforming
  - power doppler
  - CUDA
  - GPU
  - real-time
